Post an existing shift to the Job Board by creating one job board opening on it. The shift must already exist — create it first with create_shift (it may have no staff assigned), then pass its id here. A shift can carry multiple openings: call this tool again to add more openings to the same shift. Each opening may set its own time window (defaults to the shift's) and matching criteria (max_distance_km, team_segment_ids, qualification_matching). Creating an opening pins the shift to the board automatically. When the account requires a team on job board shifts, team_segment_ids is required. Use list_shifts to resolve a shift, and list_teams to resolve segment ids.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__shiftcare_au__create_job_board_posting(args: {
  // Opening end as an ISO 8601 datetime. An explicit offset is required (e.g. 2026-05-10T13:00:00+10:00); an offset-less value is rejected rather than silently zoned. Defaults to the shift's end_at when omitted.
  end_at?: string;
  // Whether this opening runs a waitlist.
  has_waitlist_enabled?: boolean;
  // Maximum travel distance (km) for a carer to be considered a match. Defaults to 100 km when omitted, so omitting it restricts matching to within 100 km.
  max_distance_km?: number;
  // How carer qualifications gate a match: `disabled` ignores qualifications (any carer qualifies); `partial` qualifies a carer who holds at least one of the shift's required qualifications; `strict` qualifies only a carer who holds all of them. Defaults to `disabled` when omitted. Only meaningful when the account has job board qualification matching enabled.
  qualification_matching?: "disabled" | "partial" | "strict";
  // ID of the existing shift to advertise. Use list_shifts to resolve a shift.
  shift_id: number;
  // Opening start as an ISO 8601 datetime. An explicit offset is required (e.g. 2026-05-10T09:00:00+10:00); an offset-less value is rejected rather than silently zoned. Defaults to the shift's start_at when omitted.
  start_at?: string;
  // Segment (team) IDs the posting is restricted to; must belong to this account. Required when the account requires a team on job board shifts.
  team_segment_ids?: Array<number>;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

