List shifts for the specified account with filters and pagination. Every query must be bounded: send from_date and to_date as a pair, or send program_id to fetch one shift series regardless of when it runs. Results are capped at 20 per page and per_page cannot be raised, so a series of more than 20 shifts spans several pages — increment page until a page returns fewer than 20, and check _metadata.total_count before reporting how many shifts a series has. One full page does not mean you have them all.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__shiftcare_au__list_shifts(args: {
  // Filter shifts from this date/datetime based on shift's approved_at (ISO 8601)
  approved_from_date?: string;
  // Filter shifts to this date/datetime based on shift's approved_at (ISO 8601)
  approved_to_date?: string;
  // Filter billable shifts only
  billable?: boolean;
  // Filter by client ID(s)
  client_id?: Array<string>;
  // Filter shifts from this date/datetime based on shift's start_at (ISO 8601, e.g. YYYY-MM-DD). Required, together with to_date, unless program_id is given.
  from_date?: string;
  // Filter by shift IDs
  ids?: Array<string>;
  // Include client information in the response
  include_clients?: boolean;
  // Include each shift's assigned staff as a staff array. In each entry, id is the staff ID (the value staff_id and get_staff take) and worker_id is the shift assignment ID, alongside scheduled and clock times and verification_status. Use it for staffing or per-staff questions instead of calling list_shift_staffs once per shift. Leave it off otherwise.
  include_staff?: boolean;
  // Filter NDIS-enabled shifts only
  ndis_enabled?: boolean;
  // Page number (default 1)
  page?: number;
  // Items per page (default 20, max 20)
  per_page?: number;
  // Filter to the shifts belonging to one program (shift series), using the program_id returned on any shift. Every shift a recurring series creates shares one program_id, so this is how to fetch a whole series server-side — do not page through the range and filter yourself. A program_id from another account, or one that does not exist, returns no shifts rather than an error.
  program_id?: number;
  // Filter by staff ID(s)
  staff_id?: Array<string>;
  // Filter by attendance review. "approved" = the attendance of at least one assigned staff member was reviewed, whatever the result (verification_status approved, rejected or rules_based), so it does not mean the attendance was accepted. "unapproved" = no attendance is reviewed yet, and the shift may still have staff assigned. To find unstaffed shifts, send include_staff and look for an empty staff list.
  status?: "approved" | "unapproved";
  // Filter shifts to this date/datetime based on shift's start_at (ISO 8601, e.g. YYYY-MM-DD). Required, together with from_date, unless program_id is given.
  to_date?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
