Update ONE existing client document's filing details — its document type, staff visibility and expiry. Returns the updated document.

REQUIRED CONFIRMATION before calling: ask the user to confirm in this format:
"Update the document [document_type] (id [id]) on [client name] — [list each change, e.g. "type -> Consent Form", "staff visibility -> visible to staff", "expiry -> 2027-03-01", "expiry -> never expires"]? This overwrites the current values and is recorded in the document's history."
Only call this tool after the user explicitly confirms.

Required: client_id (use list_clients) and id (a document id belonging to that client — use list_client_documents).
Optional, and every one of them is a change you are making: document_type_id, staff_visible, expires_at, no_expiration.

PARTIAL UPDATE: a field you omit is left exactly as it is. Send only the fields that change — do NOT re-send the document's current values, and never send a field you are unsure about.
THE FILE ITSELF CANNOT BE CHANGED HERE. A corrected file is a new upload; this tool only re-files the existing one.
document_type_id must be an active document type in this account (use list_client_document_types); an archived or another account's type is rejected. Send an empty string to unfile the document from its type.
staff_visible: true makes the document visible to staff/carers, false makes it coordinator-only. There is no third value.
expires_at is a calendar date, YYYY-MM-DD, in the ACCOUNT's time zone (not UTC) — no time component. Send an empty string ("") to clear the expiry date without marking the document as never expiring. A document with no date and no_expiration false reports expiry_status "none", but ShiftCare's own expiry reporting counts it as expired — set no_expiration: true instead if the document genuinely never expires.
no_expiration: true marks the document as never expiring and CLEARS expires_at, overriding any expires_at sent in the same call — so never send both together expecting the date to stick. To give a never-expiring document a date, send no_expiration: false and expires_at together in ONE call; that works and is the only combination in which both are honoured.
ARCHIVED DOCUMENTS ARE NOT REACHABLE: an archived document returns not-found here. Restore it first, then update.
Do not send time_zone — this tool rejects it. In the response, created_at/updated_at are UTC and expires_at is a YYYY-MM-DD date in the account's time zone.
Idempotent: calling twice with the same fields leaves the same values.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__shiftcare_au__update_client_document(args: {
  // Client id that owns the document. Use list_clients to find it.
  client_id: number;
  // Id of the DocumentType to file the document under — an ACTIVE type in this account (use list_client_document_types). An archived type or one from another account is rejected. Send an empty string to unfile the document from its type. Omit to leave the current type alone.
  document_type_id?: string;
  // New expiry date as YYYY-MM-DD, interpreted in the account's time zone (not UTC) because it is a calendar date. Send an empty string to clear it. Ignored when no_expiration is true in the same request. Omit to leave the current expiry alone.
  expires_at?: string;
  // Document id to update. Must belong to the client in client_id, and must not be archived.
  id: number;
  // True marks the document as never expiring and clears expires_at — it wins over an expires_at sent in the same request. Omit to leave it alone.
  no_expiration?: true | false;
  // True makes the document visible to staff/carers; false makes it coordinator-only (hidden from staff). This is the client profile's "Staff Visibility" setting. Omit to leave it alone.
  staff_visible?: true | false;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

